      "writtenOn": "2023-04-14T22:06:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`java_api_library` module can be considered as a combination of `droidstubs` module and `java_library` module in that it generates stubs from API text file (instead of the source java files) and also compiles the generated stubs into a jar file. However, it does not have any functionality other than generating and compiling stubs, unlike how `droidstubs` module have other functionalities (like api check, etc).\n\nThe `java_api_library` generating changes [here](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/build/orchestrator/+/2367170)(and the child changes in the stack) generates `jar` file that encompasses the full api surface, but this change enables stubs to be generated per sdk_library api scope during from-text stub build.",
      "parentUuid": "c5cbda08_7ba68f45",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1787,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 1787,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "a99fc71e5953290f22b14be30829ef75b748c5e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
