      "writtenOn": "2023-04-14T22:06:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change enforces that `java_api_library` is created inside `java_sdk_library` iff the module contributes to an api surface (specified via `apiLibGenAllowlist`). `config.SetApiLibraries([]string{\"foo\"})` in 38~40L sets `\"foo\"` as an api-surface contributing module, so the module is created in 127L. Do you believe that testing if module with the name `apiLibraryModuleName(\"foo\")` is created or not is not sufficient for testing? If so, can you suggest some additional functionalities that should be tested?",
      "parentUuid": "8e972ea1_11c5c3d3",
      "revId": "a99fc71e5953290f22b14be30829ef75b748c5e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
